> Jake Stride is a co-founder of rahd·AI, a leader in the development of 
> artificial intelligence software for oil and gas decommissioning. 
> Based in Perth, Australia, he works with engineers, data scientists 
> and industry specialists to turn fragmented operational records into 
> reliable information for planning and decision-making.
> His career spans technology strategy, industrial digital 
> transformation and software leadership. Before joining rahd·AI, Jake 
> served as Global Technology Strategist for Resources at Microsoft, led 
> digital transformation at BHP’s innovation mine, and was Chief 
> Executive Officer of Silverhorse Technologies, delivering data and 
> asset management solutions for the energy sector. He has built and 
> exited a software-as-a-service company and helped scale enterprise 
> software businesses across Australasia.
> At rahd·AI, Jake’s focus is on making AI useful in engineering 
> workflows through structured data, traceability and human validation. 
> The company’s approach brings legacy well information together into 
> verified, source-linked models that support risk assessment and 
> decommissioning readiness. His work centres on helping operators 
> understand their assets earlier, reduce uncertainty and avoid costly 
> surprises during execution.
> Jake brings a practical perspective to the adoption of AI, combining 
> commercial experience with an understanding of the data foundations 
> needed to support safer, efficient and better-informed decisions 
> across the decommissioning lifecycle.
>
